+# The Approve button spinner bug
+
+## What DaisyUI does with `btn loading`
+
+In current DaisyUI (v4+), `loading` is **not** a button modifier — it's a
+standalone **component class** meant for its own element, e.g.
+`<span class="loading loading-spinner"></span>`. The class turns *whatever
+element it's on* into the spinner glyph itself. Roughly:
+
+```css
+.loading {
+  pointer-events: none;
+  display: inline-block;
+  aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;            /* force a square box */
+  width: 1.5rem;                  /* default size (loading-md) */
+  background-color: currentColor; /* fill the whole box with the text color */
+  mask-repeat: no-repeat;
+  mask-position: center;
+  mask-size: 100%;
+  mask-image: url("data:image/svg+xml,...animated spinner...");
+}
+```
+
+So by putting `loading` **on the `<button>` itself**, the teammate told
+DaisyUI "this button *is* the spinner." The consequences map exactly to the
+QA report:
+
+- **Label disappears.** The button gets `background-color: currentColor`
+  masked by the spinner SVG (`mask-image` + `mask-size: 100%`). The mask clips
+  the element's paint to the spinner shape — the real text node
+  (`"Approving..."`) is still in the DOM but is completely painted over /
+  masked out, so nothing readable shows. You only see the masked fill, which
+  is the spinner.
+- **One big spinner filling the button.** `mask-size: 100%` scales the spinner
+  to the full element, and `aspect-ratio: 1 / 1` forces the box square. The
+  button's own width/height now drive the spinner size, so the spinner is as
+  large as the button.
+- **Layout jumps.** `aspect-ratio: 1 / 1` + the component `width` override the
+  button's normal sizing, so its dimensions change the instant `isPending`
+  flips — the box resizes and neighbors shift.
+- **Desktop and mobile alike**, because none of this is breakpoint-dependent —
+  it's just the wrong class on the wrong element.
+
+(The old `btn loading` behavior from DaisyUI v2/v3 no longer exists; the class
+was repurposed into a standalone component, which is why this pattern that
+"used to work" now eats the button.)
+
+## The fix — idiomatic DaisyUI / Scaffold-ETH 2 pattern
+
+Keep `loading loading-spinner` on a **separate child `<span>`** next to the
+text, and size it small (`loading-sm`) so it sits inline. Never put `loading`
+on the `btn` itself.
+
+```jsx
+<button className="btn btn-primary" disabled={isPending}>
+  {isPending && <span className="loading loading-spinner loading-sm"></span>}
+  {isPending ? "Approving..." : "Approve"}
+</button>
+```
+
+Why this is correct:
+
+- The spinner is its own element, so `aspect-ratio: 1/1` and `currentColor`
+  masking apply only to the little `<span>`, not the button.
+- `loading-sm` keeps it a small inline glyph; the button's flex layout
+  (`btn` is `display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap`) places it neatly
+  to the left of the text.
+- The `"Approving..."` label stays fully visible.
+- No dimension change from a forced square aspect ratio, so no layout jump —
+  the button just grows by the width of a small spinner + gap.
+
+This is the exact pattern Scaffold-ETH 2 uses across its own components (e.g.
+`<span className="loading loading-spinner loading-sm"></span>` inside a
+`btn btn-primary`).
+
+### Optional refinement
+
+To avoid any width shift at all, you can reserve the label and only toggle the
+spinner's visibility, or use `min-w-*` on the button. But the snippet above is
+the standard, minimal SE-2 idiom and resolves the reported bug.

